# Post-PR cleanup

When you help the user create a PR (via `gh pr create`, `git push` of a new
branch, or similar), schedule a check N minutes later. If the chat is
still active at that point, verify whether the PR merged and clean up
local branches.

## Timer (configurable)

Default: **30 minutes**. Override via user instruction in the same turn
("create the PR and check in 10 min", "no auto-check, I'll handle it").

Heuristic suggestions (apply silently; mention only if the user asks):

| Situation | Suggested delay |
|---|---|
| `gh pr merge --auto` enabled + small diff + green CI history | 5–10 min |
| Solo-owner / personal repo, no reviewers | 5 min |
| Roblox infra repo with 1–2 reviewers (normal case) | 30 min (default) |
| Repo with slow CI (prophase e2e, eecd e2e) | 45–60 min |
| Cross-team / many-reviewers PR | 90 min, or skip auto-check entirely |

If unsure, ask the user once at PR-creation time: "check in X min?"
After that, don't re-prompt for the same PR.

## Trigger

After a successful `gh pr create`, capture the PR URL/number, repo slug,
and chosen delay (in seconds), then schedule a self-notification:

```bash
# Reminder fires once after <delay>s. The sentinel string is matched by
# notify_on_output so the agent gets woken up.
sleep <delay> && echo "PR-CLEANUP-CHECK <repo-slug> <pr-number>"
```

Set `block_until_ms: 0` (immediate background) and configure
`notify_on_output` with `pattern: "PR-CLEANUP-CHECK"` and a short reason
like `PR ready to verify`.

## When the reminder fires

1. Check merge state, do not assume merged just because time passed:

   ```bash
   gh pr view <pr-number> --repo <repo-slug> \
     --json state,mergedAt,baseRefName,headRefName
   ```

2. If `state != MERGED`: report current state to the user, ask whether
   to reschedule another 30-min check, close, or wait. Do nothing else.

3. If `state == MERGED`, in the repo's working tree (default to the
   workspace root that originated the PR; ask if ambiguous):

   ```bash
   git checkout <baseRefName>   # NOT hardcoded main/master - release branches matter
   git pull --ff-only            # the default-branch sync cron also does this hourly; safe to repeat
   gprune -f                     # ~/work/dotfiles/zsh/aliases.sh: fetch --prune + delete [gone] branches
   ```

4. If `gprune` isn't on PATH (non-interactive shells don't source
   `aliases.sh`), fall back to the raw one-liner:

   ```bash
   git fetch --prune && \
     git branch -vv | awk '/: gone\]/ {print $1}' | xargs -r git branch -D
   ```

## Discipline

- Only switch branches if the working tree is clean
  (`git status --porcelain` empty). Otherwise report and stop.
- Never `push --force`, never touch remote branches.
- This only fires while the chat is active. If the user closes the
  chat, the timer dies with it. No recovery on next session unless
  the user asks.
- The hourly `~/bin/sync-default-branches` launchd job already handles
  fast-forward of default branches across all `~/work/` repos. This
  rule adds the per-PR-merge prune step the cron doesn't do.
